<!DOCTYPE reference PUBLIC "-//OASIS//DTD DITA Reference//EN" "reference.dtd">
<reference id="zero-latency-monitor-settings" xml:lang="en-us" otherprops="draft" props="ai-authored" class="- topic/topic       reference/reference "><title class="- topic/title ">Zero-Latency Monitor settings</title><shortdesc class="- topic/shortdesc ">Review the options and default values for each setting on the Zero-Latency Monitor settings screen.</shortdesc><refbody class="- topic/body        reference/refbody "><section class="- topic/section "><title class="- topic/title ">Settings options</title><p class="- topic/p ">Open the settings screen from the quick access toolbar. Recording pauses while the settings screen is open.</p><table class="- topic/table "><tgroup cols="4" class="- topic/tgroup "><colspec colname="c1" colnum="1" class="- topic/colspec "/><colspec colname="c2" colnum="2" class="- topic/colspec "/><colspec colname="c3" colnum="3" class="- topic/colspec "/><colspec colname="c4" colnum="4" class="- topic/colspec "/><thead class="- topic/thead "><row class="- topic/row "><entry class="- topic/entry "><p class="- topic/p ">Setting</p></entry><entry class="- topic/entry "><p class="- topic/p ">Options</p></entry><entry class="- topic/entry "><p class="- topic/p ">Default</p></entry><entry class="- topic/entry "><p class="- topic/p ">Notes</p></entry></row></thead><tbody class="- topic/tbody "><row class="- topic/row "><entry class="- topic/entry "><p class="- topic/p "><uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">Loop recording</uicontrol></p></entry><entry class="- topic/entry "><p class="- topic/p ">1 minute, 2 minutes, 3 minutes</p></entry><entry class="- topic/entry "><p class="- topic/p ">1 minute</p></entry><entry class="- topic/entry "><p class="- topic/p ">Sets the recording duration.</p></entry></row><row class="- topic/row "><entry class="- topic/entry "><p class="- topic/p "><uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">Flameout setting</uicontrol></p></entry><entry class="- topic/entry "><p class="- topic/p ">Parking monitor switch, low voltage protection, monitoring time</p></entry><entry class="- topic/entry "><p class="- topic/p ">Not specified</p></entry><entry class="- topic/entry "><p class="- topic/p ">Controls how the monitor behaves after the vehicle is switched off.</p></entry></row><row class="- topic/row "><entry class="- topic/entry "><p class="- topic/p "><uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">Mic switch</uicontrol></p></entry><entry class="- topic/entry "><p class="- topic/p ">On, off</p></entry><entry class="- topic/entry "><p class="- topic/p ">Off</p></entry><entry class="- topic/entry "><p class="- topic/p ">Only Channel 1 has audio. When on, the Channel 1 camera records video and audio together.</p></entry></row><row class="- topic/row "><entry class="- topic/entry "><p class="- topic/p "><uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">Sensitivity</uicontrol></p></entry><entry class="- topic/entry "><p class="- topic/p ">Off, low, medium, high</p></entry><entry class="- topic/entry "><p class="- topic/p ">Off</p></entry><entry class="- topic/entry "><p class="- topic/p ">See "About sensitivity."</p></entry></row><row class="- topic/row "><entry class="- topic/entry "><p class="- topic/p "><uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">Split setting</uicontrol></p></entry><entry class="- topic/entry "><p class="- topic/p ">Two divisions, Three divisions (three layouts), Four divisions (two layouts)</p></entry><entry class="- topic/entry "><p class="- topic/p ">Four divisions (CH1 and CH4 on top, CH2 and CH3 on the bottom)</p></entry><entry class="- topic/entry "><p class="- topic/p ">Tap the icon in the top-left corner to finish.</p></entry></row><row class="- topic/row "><entry class="- topic/entry "><p class="- topic/p "><uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">Lens resolution</uicontrol></p></entry><entry class="- topic/entry "><p class="- topic/p ">1080p 30fps, 720p 25fps, 720p 30fps, Cvbs pal, Cvbs ntsc</p></entry><entry class="- topic/entry "><p class="- topic/p ">720p 30fps</p></entry><entry class="- topic/entry "><p class="- topic/p ">All connected cameras must have the same specifications. Mixed cameras can make the display appear abnormal.</p></entry></row><row class="- topic/row "><entry class="- topic/entry "><p class="- topic/p "><uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">Video resolution</uicontrol></p></entry><entry class="- topic/entry "><p class="- topic/p ">720p, Cvbs</p></entry><entry class="- topic/entry "><p class="- topic/p ">720p</p></entry><entry class="- topic/entry "><p class="- topic/p ">Not applicable</p></entry></row><row class="- topic/row "><entry class="- topic/entry "><p class="- topic/p "><uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">Screen sleep</uicontrol></p></entry><entry class="- topic/entry "><p class="- topic/p ">Shut down, 30 seconds, 60 seconds</p></entry><entry class="- topic/entry "><p class="- topic/p ">Shut down</p></entry><entry class="- topic/entry "><p class="- topic/p ">Recording continues while the backlight is off. Tap the screen to restore it.</p></entry></row><row class="- topic/row "><entry class="- topic/entry "><p class="- topic/p "><uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">Volume</uicontrol></p></entry><entry class="- topic/entry "><p class="- topic/p ">Off, low, medium, high</p></entry><entry class="- topic/entry "><p class="- topic/p ">Medium</p></entry><entry class="- topic/entry "><p class="- topic/p ">Raises the startup sound and touch feedback sound.</p></entry></row><row class="- topic/row "><entry class="- topic/entry "><p class="- topic/p "><uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">Brightness</uicontrol></p></entry><entry class="- topic/entry "><p class="- topic/p ">Low, middle, high</p></entry><entry class="- topic/entry "><p class="- topic/p ">High</p></entry><entry class="- topic/entry "><p class="- topic/p ">Not applicable</p></entry></row><row class="- topic/row "><entry class="- topic/entry "><p class="- topic/p "><uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">Language</uicontrol></p></entry><entry class="- topic/entry "><p class="- topic/p ">Simplified Chinese, Traditional Chinese, English, Korean, German</p></entry><entry class="- topic/entry "><p class="- topic/p ">Simplified Chinese</p></entry><entry class="- topic/entry "><p class="- topic/p ">Not applicable</p></entry></row><row class="- topic/row "><entry class="- topic/entry "><p class="- topic/p "><uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">Clock</uicontrol></p></entry><entry class="- topic/entry "><p class="- topic/p ">Year, month, day, hour, minutes, seconds</p></entry><entry class="- topic/entry "><p class="- topic/p ">Not applicable</p></entry><entry class="- topic/entry "><p class="- topic/p ">Use the up and down arrows to set each value. Tap outside the screen to save and exit.</p></entry></row><row class="- topic/row "><entry class="- topic/entry "><p class="- topic/p "><uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">Key tone</uicontrol></p></entry><entry class="- topic/entry "><p class="- topic/p ">Open, close</p></entry><entry class="- topic/entry "><p class="- topic/p ">Open</p></entry><entry class="- topic/entry "><p class="- topic/p ">Turns the sound on or off when you tap the screen.</p></entry></row><row class="- topic/row "><entry class="- topic/entry "><p class="- topic/p "><uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">Mirror setting</uicontrol></p></entry><entry class="- topic/entry "><p class="- topic/p ">Horizontal mirror or vertical flip, for each channel (CH1 to CH4)</p></entry><entry class="- topic/entry "><p class="- topic/p ">All off</p></entry><entry class="- topic/entry "><p class="- topic/p ">Tap a channel to enable the setting. Tap again to disable it.</p></entry></row><row class="- topic/row "><entry class="- topic/entry "><p class="- topic/p "><uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">Info inquiry</uicontrol></p></entry><entry class="- topic/entry "><p class="- topic/p ">Not applicable</p></entry><entry class="- topic/entry "><p class="- topic/p ">Not applicable</p></entry><entry class="- topic/entry "><p class="- topic/p ">Shows the total SD card capacity and the percentage used by ordinary videos, emergency videos, and pictures.</p></entry></row><row class="- topic/row "><entry class="- topic/entry "><p class="- topic/p "><uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">Format</uicontrol></p></entry><entry class="- topic/entry "><p class="- topic/p ">Not applicable</p></entry><entry class="- topic/entry "><p class="- topic/p ">Not applicable</p></entry><entry class="- topic/entry "><p class="- topic/p ">Deletes all files on the SD card, including emergency videos.</p></entry></row><row class="- topic/row "><entry class="- topic/entry "><p class="- topic/p "><uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">System reset</uicontrol></p></entry><entry class="- topic/entry "><p class="- topic/p ">Not applicable</p></entry><entry class="- topic/entry "><p class="- topic/p ">Not applicable</p></entry><entry class="- topic/entry "><p class="- topic/p ">Restores all settings to factory defaults.</p></entry></row></tbody></tgroup></table><draft-comment author="Claude Code" time="2026-10-01" disposition="issue" class="- topic/draft-comment ">Open items after reviewing the manual screenshots. (1) Lens: the manual text is empty. A second interface version in the manual shows a version icon and an AI Switch instead of Lens and Key tone, so confirm which version ships. (2) Lens resolution: the manual text says the default is "720P 30fps tvi", but the screen shows "720p 30fps" and also a "1080p 30fps" option (seen in the version with the AI Switch). (3) Flameout: the manual text says customization is not supported, but the screen shows adjustment arrows with 11.2 V, 22.8 V, and 05S. (4) Default language: the manual text says Simplified Chinese, but the screenshot highlights English, and German is listed on screen but not in the text. (5) Info inquiry is called TF information in the other interface version, which also has a version icon. (6) CERT-2731 notes that sample units may be old stock, so options and defaults can differ from the manual.</draft-comment></section><section class="- topic/section "><title class="- topic/title ">About sensitivity</title><p class="- topic/p ">When sensitivity is off, the device does not trigger an emergency recording, even in a severe collision. Low, medium, and high progressively lower the collision threshold for triggering an emergency recording. When one triggers, the monitor starts a 20-second emergency recording, shows a "Locked recording!" message, and shows a red locked icon in the top-right corner of the screen.</p><draft-comment author="Claude Code" time="2026-10-01" disposition="issue" class="- topic/draft-comment ">Sensitivity message: the manual text says "Video Locked!", but the screenshot shows "Locked recording!". Confirm the exact message.</draft-comment></section></refbody></reference>